 the supplied research, but that does not demonstrate rxn_005 on this multifunctional substrate. Replacing a photoreductant also does not automatically replace any sulfur-dependent substrate chemistry in a homologation sequence. Ferrocyanide is mentioned at pathway level without a reaction-specific loading, role, or operating protocol. The final hydrolysis sequence remains plausible but unvalidated under stated environmental conditions.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_003\",\n        \"rxn_005\",\n        \"rxn_013\",\n        \"rxn_016\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Demonstrate the resolved homologation sequence using sulfite/ferrocyanide and this substrate; distinguish electron-donor substitution from any requirement for sulfur-containing intermediates.\",\n        \"Declare ferrocyanide participation and specify irradiation, catalyst loading, turnover, speciation, and environmental availability.\",\n        \"Establish an experimentally supported hydrolysis window that produces and preserves free arginine.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.25,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.65,\n        \"rxn_016\": 0.65\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.45,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.57,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.5,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.28,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.38,\n      \"feedback\": \"Guanidinylation before alpha-amino-group installation avoids one important selectivity problem. Nevertheless, rxn_006 leaves the essential carbon-skeleton construction unresolved while the terminal amine remains unprotected. Relevant aminoaldehyde intermediates can cyclize, and cyanohydrin equilibration can expose aldehydes to competing cyanamide chemistry. Therefore, rxn_008 cannot be assumed to gi