asking, guanidinylation efficiency, rxn_015, and final hydrolysis remain unresolved.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_023", "rxn_014", "rxn_015", "rxn_016", "rxn_017", "rxn_018", "rxn_019", "rxn_020"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_011", "mol_021", "mol_022", "mol_026"]}, {"pathway_id": "P4", "name": "Guanidinylation at the hydroxythioamide", "description": "Exploratory functional-group-ordering variant. Guanidine is installed after sulfur addition but before proposed deoxygenation. The terminal amine may be more nucleophilic than the thioamide nitrogen, but sulfur-centred competition is untested. Neither the selectivity of rxn_024 nor the productive photochemistry of rxn_015 is established.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_024", "rxn_015", "rxn_016", "rxn_017", "rxn_018", "rxn_019", "rxn_020"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_012", "mol_022", "mol_023", "mol_026"]}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "name": "Guanidinylation after chain extension but before the second aldehyde", "description": "Conditional late-single-amine variant. It avoids exposing guanidine to rxn_006 while installing it before the cyclization-prone gamma-aminoaldehyde stage. Its main upstream failure point is the unverified amino-hydroxythioamide deoxygenation; guanidinylation of mol_013 and downstream hydrolysis also require validation.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_025", "rxn_016", "rxn_017", "rxn_018", "rxn_019", "rxn_020"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_012", "mol_013", "mol_023", "mol_026"]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "name": "Guanidinylation at the transient C4 aminoaldehyde", "description": "Low-priority kinetic-competition hypothesis. It requires cyanamide guanidinylation to access productive linear material despite rapid cyclic-imine chemistry. This is not an asserted available aldehyde inventory. In addition to rxn_006, both open-chain aldehyde capture and free-arginine release remain unresolved.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_026", "rxn_017", "rxn_018", "rxn_019", "rxn_020"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_013", "mol_014", "mol_024", "mol_026"]}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "name": "Guanidinylation of the final cyanohydrin before Strecker amination", "description": "Conditional route that installs guanidine immediately before the alpha-amino group. It avoids direct competition between two primary amines but requires selective open-chain cyanohydrin capture and persistence. Cyanohydrin reversal can reintroduce the cyclic-imine problem. The scaffold and hydrolysis gaps are not resolved by this ordering.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_027", "rxn_018", "rxn_019", "rxn_020"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_014", "mol_015", "mol_025", "mol_026"]}, {"pathway_id": "P8", "name": "Guanidinylation of ornithine alpha-aminonitrile", "description": "Conditional diamino-nitrile route. Guanidine is installed only after backbone construction and Strecker amination. This avoids guanidino exposure to scaffold photochemistry but requires unproven delta-versus-alpha guanidinylation selectivity, followed by guanidino-preserving nitrile and amide hydrolysis.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_028", "rxn_019", "rxn_020"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_015", "mol_016", "mol_026", "mol_027"]}, {"pathway_id": "P9", "name": "Guanidinylation after nitrile hydration", "description": "Conditional ornithinamide route. Hydration is completed before guanidine installation, reducing its exposure to nitrile-processing conditions. The alpha-amino group remains unprotected, so delta selectivity is not supplied by the amide. Controlled ornithinamide accumulation, rxn_029 selectivity, and rxn_020 target release remain unverified.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010", "rxn_029", "rxn_020"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_016", "mol_017", "mol_027"]}, {"pathway_id": "P10", "name": "Guanidinylation of fully hydrolysed free ornithine", "description": "Conditional post-hoc monomer route. All carboxyl-group processing precedes guanidinylation, eliminating the requirement that a guanidino group survive those hydrolysis operations. It retains the upstream scaffold and open-chain-selection gaps and requires experimentally unestablished delta-selective cyanamide conversion of free ornithine. Protein guanidination and discharge ornithine detections do not close that final gap.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010", "rxn_011", "rxn_030"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_016", "mol_017", "mol_018"]}], "hub_molecules": ["mol_001", "mol_003", "mol_004", "mol_005", "mol_006", "mol_007", "mol_009", "mol_010", "mol_011", "mol_012", "mol_013", "mol_014", "mol_015", "mol_016", "mol_017", "mol_020", "mol_021", "mol_022", "mol_023", "mol_024", "mol_025", "mol_026", "mol_027", "mol_028"], "convergence_points": [{"molecule_id": "mol_020", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_012", "rxn_022"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_013"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_021", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_013", "rxn_023"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_014"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_022", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_014", "rxn_024"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_015"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_023", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_015", "rxn_025"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_016"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_024", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_016", "rxn_026"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_017"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_025", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_017", "rxn_027"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_018"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_026", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_018", "rxn_028"], "outgoin